  "critical": false,
  "description": "Design and erection of overhead contact systems (catenary) that supply electric power to pantographs on moving locomotives. Covers tensioning, span lengths, contact-wire wave mechanics, and the trade-off between DC low-voltage (600-3000 V) and AC high-voltage (15 kV/16.7 Hz or 25 kV/50-60 Hz) systems. The defining infrastructure choice that distinguishes mainline electric railways from diesel or third-rail metros.",
